    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Fills missing values with the mean, median, mode, a constant, previous / next value or interpolation, optionally within groups, with indicator fields and a summary.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Cleansing",
    "tags": [
        "imputation",
        "missing values",
        "nulls",
        "fill",
        "median",
        "interpolate",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Fills missing values so that totals, averages, charts and models are not thrown off by gaps.\n\n**Number fields**: mean, median, mode, a constant, the previous or next value, or linear interpolation between neighbours.\n**Text fields**: the most common value, a constant (such as *Unknown*), or the previous or next value.\n\n- **Within groups**: compute the fill value per group, such as the median floor area *per property type and region*, falling back to the overall value when a group has no data at all\n- **Order** for previous / next / interpolation, such as by date within each sensor\n- **Sentinel values** such as -999 or 9999 can be treated as missing too\n- **Indicator fields** (`<field> Was Imputed`, 1 or 0) so filled values stay visible and can be excluded later\n- Integer fields stay whole numbers\n\nThe second output summarises each field: method, missing before, imputed, still missing and the value used.",
